m the five known scores:  \n- 89  \n- 71  \n- 92  \n- 100  \n- 86  \n\nThe **lowest** is **71**.\n\nSo, if Brinley gets a score $ x $ on the sixth test, the **lowest of the six scores** will be:\n\n- If $ x < 71 $, then the lowest is $ x $\n- If $ x \\geq 71 $, then the lowest is still **71**\n\nSo, we need to consider **two cases**:\n\n---\n\n### **Case 1: $ x \\geq 71 $**\n\nThen the lowest score is **71**, and we remove it.\n\nSo, the five scores we average are:\n\n- 89  \n- 92  \n- 100  \n- 86  \n- $ x $\n\nLet\u2019s compute the sum of these five scores:\n\n$$\n89 + 92 + 100 + 86 + x = 367 + x\n$$\n\nWe want the average of these five to be **93**:\n\n$$\n\\frac{367 + x}{5} = 93\n$$\n\nMultiply both sides by 5:\n\n$$\n367 + x = 465\n$$\n\n$$\nx = 465 - 367 = 98\n$$\n\nSo, if $ x = 98 $, then the average of the five highest scores is 93.\n\nBut we must check if this is valid under the assumption that $ x \\geq 71 $, which it is.\n\n\u2705 **Valid solution: $ x = 98 $**\n\n---\n\n### **Case 2: $ x < 71 $**\n\nThen the lowest score is $ x $, and we remove it.\n\nSo, the five scores we average are:\n\n- 89  \n- 71  \n- 92  \n- 100  \n- 86\n\nSum = $ 89 + 71 + 92 + 100 + 86 = 438 $\n\nAverage = $ \\frac{438}{5} = 87.6 $\n\nThis is **less than 93**, so this case **does not work**.\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\nBrinley needs to score **98** on the sixth test to get an average of 93 after removing the lowest score.\n\n$$\n\\boxed{98}\n$$", "decode_seconds": 5.584825349971652, "draft_calls": 150, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 114, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "0a4f3a2a3c16c7a936e9bb48040a8a34a5ebd624b90afc44855d7cc390241de1", "method": "relay_cropped", "output_hash": "270fd23661c8b94c581a24368ea6d6c927e07a16e5596e7aba52b3eac62777c6", "output_tokens": 785, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23689032192, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23915921408, "problem_id": "gsm8k/844d7a1768c19756", "profile_regions_ms": {"draft": 945.6878380775452, "prefill_full_target":